  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Intercept and play forward first time",
  "description": "Play 6 v 6 with goalkeepers on a pitch of about 50 × 60 metres. The diagram shows four outfield players per team. The focus is the interception: whoever cuts out a pass should, when possible, play the ball on forward with the same touch and start the counter-attack at once.\n\nA goal from a counter where the interception and the first pass were the same touch is worth three points. A normal goal is worth one. Encourage a long pass in behind the opponents when a teammate has already started running. The coach stands on the side and plays in a new ball when it goes out.\n\nPlay offside if you do in matches – then the run in behind must be timed. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Read the pass early and step in front of the receiver, not behind."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Decide before the ball arrives where it should go. Look up before you intercept."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Teammates start their runs as soon as they see the interception coming."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you can't play forward first time, take a safe touch and keep the ball."
    }
  ],
